t foresight and that the costs of failure are always internalizable. I assume that autonomous military agents operate in high-entropy environments where failures propagate faster than human intervention can correct them. If this assumption proves wrong—if AI systems are inherently self-correcting—then my push for rigid oversight would be an unnecessary constraint. However, given current evidence on cascading algorithmic failures, the risk of inaction remains unacceptably high, necessitating the implementation of the Autonomous Military Agent Governance Framework (AMAGF) as a non-negotiable prerequisite for deployment. 🛡️",
